omx-clap-host (0.14.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * libomx-clap-core holds /dev/cpu_dma_latency while a hosted plugin is
    active, at 10 us by default (C1 only), 0 for no idle state, or off: one
    descriptor per process, opened at the first activate and closed at the
    last, so a crash restores the machine's default. A device that cannot be
    opened is reported by code, hosting.idle.hold-refused, declared in this
    tree's data/hosting.json, and the host runs on. omx-clap-host takes
    --idle-hold and an idle_hold command; its packages ship a udev rule
    giving the audio group the device. The calls are in the version node
    OMX_CLAP_CORE_0.14. The library ABI is 16.
  * The hosting codes are this tree's: omx-contract's 16 data/hosting files
    moved here byte for byte, installed under contract.d/3/omx-clap-core/
    hosting/ and rendered as omx_clap_core_vocabulary.h and the omx-clap-core-
    vocabulary TypeScript module, the OMX_HOSTING_ names unchanged. The six
    retired codes are removed (72 codes are left) and featuresMissingAtLoad is
    featuresMissing. omx-clap-scan --fields clap:<path>#<id> | lv2:<uri>
    writes one plugin's field dump for plugin-hostd's format tables, an LV2
    plugin read from the adapter's lilv world with its binary never opened.
    omx-contract 3.0.0 or newer.

